  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Raja Khadarvalli Babu vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 31 January, 2023 Author: R. Raghunandan Rao Bench: R. Raghunandan Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice R. Raghunandan Rao Writ Petition No.1699 of 2023 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioner being aggrieved by the proceedings of the 3rd respondent dated 04.11.2019 in C.No.105/GL- SDOA/2019, opening a suspect sheet against the petitioner and others has approached this Court, by way of the present writ petition.",
    "arguments": "2. Sri Raja Reddy Koneti, learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the said suspect sheet had been opened against the petitioner on the ground that the petitioner was involved in Crime No.92 of 2018 on the file of A.S.Peta Police Station for offences under Sections 353, 272, 273 r/w 34 of I.P.C and Section 59(iv) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He contends that no such suspect sheet could have been opened or continued against the petitioner on the basis of the alleged involvement in the said crime.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. Sri Raja Reddy Koneti, learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the said suspect sheet had been opened against the petitioner on the ground that the petitioner was involved in Crime No.92 of 2018 on the file of A.S.Peta Police Station for offences under Sections 353, 272, 273 r/w 34 of I.P.C and Section 59(iv) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. He contends that no such suspect sheet could have been opened or continued against the petitioner on the basis of the alleged involvement in the said crime.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
